.TH tee 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
tee \- copy standard input to standard output and to files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tee
[\fB\-a\fR] [\fB\-i\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tee
reads standard input and writes it both to standard output and to each
named
.IR file .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Append to the files rather than truncating them.
.TP
.B \-i
Ignore interrupts.
.SH NOTES
Up to 17 files may be named.
.PP
.B \-a
is done by opening the file and seeking to the end once, not with
.BR O_APPEND ,
so two
.B tee
processes appending to the same file overwrite each other rather than
interleaving.  A file that does not exist yet is created either way.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# ls -l | tee listing
# cc prog.c 2>&1 | tee errs
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cat (1)
